@page "/components/ai/form"
@implements IAsyncDisposable

<PageOutlet Url="components/ai/form"
            Title="AiForm"
            Description="BitAiForm renders a form a model proposed - from fields or a JSON Schema - out of the core inputs, validates it on the client and submits the corrected values back." />

<DemoPage Name="AiForm"
          SecondaryNames="@(["SchemaForm"])"
          Description="BitAiForm renders a form the model proposed, for the user to check and submit. Rather than calling a tool with arguments it guessed, a model describes a form - as fields, or as the same JSON Schema it already uses for tool arguments - the user corrects it, and the corrected values are what execute. Every field is a core input (BitTextField, BitNumberField, BitCheckbox, BitDropdown, BitDatePicker, BitTimePicker), nested objects become groups and arrays lists the user adds to, and validation happens here rather than in the model. Fields appear as the schema streams in, and what the user typed is kept."
          Parameters="componentParameters"
          SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
          SubEnums="componentSubEnums"
          PublicMembers="componentPublicMembers"
          CssVariables="componentCssVariables"
          GitHubAIUrl="Form/BitAiForm.razor"
          GitHubDemoUrl="AI/Form/BitAiFormDemo.razor">
    <NotesTemplate>
        <BitText>
            To use this component, you need to install the
            <BitLink Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Bit.BlazorUI.AI" Target="_blank">
                <BitTag Reversed
                        Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI"
                        Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground"
                        IconName="@BitIconName.NavigateExternalInline" />
            </BitLink>
            nuget package, as described in the Optional steps of the
            <BitLink Href="/getting-started">Getting started</BitLink> page.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            BitAiForm needs nothing but its <b>Definition</b>: no session and no transport. A form a model proposes usually
            arrives as a structured output part whose JSON Schema an app turns into a definition with
            <b>BitAiFormDefinition.FromJsonSchema</b>, in a renderer registered for that schema - see
            <BitLink Href="/components/ai/structureddataview">BitAiStructuredDataView</BitLink> and the
            <BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/forms">Forms</BitLink> scenario. Its default button texts (Submit, Cancel), the
            Submitted confirmation, the texts of its lists and the validation messages come from the strings in force
            (<b>BitAiStrings</b>, listed in the tables below), which a
            <BitLink Href="/components/ai/optionsprovider">BitAiOptionsProvider</BitLink> or <b>ConfigureUi</b> localizes.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            <b>Security</b>: validation runs here because a model asked to check its own output will sometimes say yes when the
            answer is no - and the values a user submits are still input: validate them again wherever they execute. A
            <b>pattern</b> a model wrote is matched under a timeout, so a catastrophic one fails the field instead of freezing
            the page; one that is not a valid regular expression is ignored.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            <b>Accessibility</b>: each field is a core input with its own label, description and error message, which its
            control points at through <b>aria-describedby</b> while it says <b>aria-invalid</b>. A nested object and a list are a
            <b>fieldset</b> with a <b>legend</b>; an entry of a list of objects is a group named after the list and its place
            (Speakers 2), an entry of a list of values an input named the same way, and its remove button says which entry it
            removes. Once an entry is removed the focus moves to the remove button now in its place (or that of the new last
            entry), or to the add button of a list left empty, rather than falling back to the top of the page. The errors the form renders itself (a list's, a
            checkbox's) are announced as alerts.
        </BitText>
    </NotesTemplate>
    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
            <div>
                A <b>BitAiFormDefinition</b> is a title, a description and its <b>Fields</b>, each a <b>BitAiFormField</b> named
                after the key its value is submitted under (and labelled after it, unless it has a <b>Label</b>). <b>OnSubmit</b>
                is handed the values of a valid form, as text keyed by field name.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm Definition="contactForm" OnSubmit="values => contactValues = values" />
            <br />
            @if (contactValues is not null)
            {
                <ul>
                    @foreach (var (key, value) in contactValues)
                    {
                        <li><b>@key</b>: @value</li>
                    }
                </ul>
            }
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Field types" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2">
            <div>
                <b>Type</b> picks the control, a <b>BitAiFieldType</b>: a text box, a multi-line one, a number, a checkbox, a
                dropdown over <b>Options</b> (labelled by <b>OptionLabels</b>), a date, a date and time, a time, an email, a URL
                or a password. <b>Value</b> prefills it, <b>Placeholder</b> and <b>Description</b> help with it. Whatever the
                control, the value is submitted as invariant text: <b>2</b>, <b>true</b>, <b>2026-10-23</b>, <b>14:30</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm Definition="typesForm" OnSubmit="values => typesValues = values" />
            <br />
            @if (typesValues is not null)
            {
                <ul>
                    @foreach (var (key, value) in typesValues)
                    {
                        <li><b>@key</b>: @value</li>
                    }
                </ul>
            }
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="JSON Schema" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3">
            <div>
                <b>BitAiFormDefinition.FromJsonSchema</b> builds a form from a JSON Schema object, the vocabulary a model already
                uses for tool arguments: <b>type</b>, <b>format</b>, <b>enum</b> with <b>enumNames</b>, <b>default</b>,
                <b>title</b>, <b>description</b>, <b>required</b> and the rest. A second argument prefills it, ahead of the
                defaults. <b>OnSubmitJson</b> hands the values back as JSON of the shape of the schema, numbers and booleans
                typed as such.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm Definition="bookingForm" OnSubmitJson="json => bookingJson = json" />
            <br />
            <BitAiJsonView Value="bookingJson" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Schema keywords" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4">
            <div>
                The rest of the vocabulary <b>FromJsonSchema</b> reads, one property each in the form below:
                a <b>const</b> is a read-only field holding its value (<b>Event</b>), and so is a <b>readOnly</b> property with a
                <b>default</b> (<b>Seat</b>); a <b>oneOf</b> - or <b>anyOf</b> - of <b>const</b> values is a dropdown labelled by
                their titles (<b>Ticket</b>); <b>format</b> <b>date-time</b> is a date and time picker and <b>password</b> a masked
                input; a <b>type</b> that also allows <b>"null"</b> (<b>["string", "null"]</b>, an <b>anyOf</b> with a null
                alternative, or OpenAPI's <b>nullable: true</b>) makes a field optional even when it is <b>required</b>
                (<b>Phone</b>), and <b>examples</b> become its placeholder; a local <b>$ref</b> into <b>$defs</b> (or
                <b>definitions</b>) is followed, with a <b>title</b> or <b>description</b> written beside it winning over the
                target's (<b>Contact</b>). <b>x-enumNames</b> labels an <b>enum</b> like <b>enumNames</b>, and the draft-4
                boolean <b>exclusiveMinimum</b> / <b>exclusiveMaximum</b> are read too. A keyword of the wrong kind is ignored and an
                unknown shape falls back to a text box, since a model wrote the schema.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm Definition="seatForm" OnSubmitJson="json => seatJson = json" />
            <br />
            <BitAiJsonView Value="seatJson" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Validation" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
            <div>
                Submit checks every field: <b>required</b>, <b>minLength</b> / <b>maxLength</b>, <b>pattern</b>,
                <b>minimum</b> / <b>maximum</b> and their exclusive forms, whole numbers (<b>integer</b>), <b>multipleOf</b>, the
                format of an email, a web address (an absolute http or https URL) or a date, and a choice the options do not offer.
                Each error is shown on its field - whose input points at it through <b>aria-describedby</b> and says
                <b>aria-invalid</b> - and clears as the field is edited; <b>OnSubmit</b> is raised only once the form is valid.
                The messages are the validation strings of the AI options (see the table below). Press <b>Sign up</b> with the
                form empty, then fix it: try a username with capitals, an age of 17, a website without its https://, and a donation
                of 7 or of 1000.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm Definition="signUpForm" OnSubmit="values => signUpValues = values" />
            <br />
            @if (signUpValues is not null)
            {
                <div>Valid: <b>@string.Join(", ", signUpValues.Select(v => $"{v.Key} = {v.Value}"))</b></div>
            }
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Nested objects & lists" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
            <div>
                An <b>object</b> with <b>properties</b> becomes a group of fields (<b>BitAiFieldType.Object</b>) and an
                <b>array</b> a list the user adds entries to and removes them from (<b>BitAiFieldType.Array</b>): a list of
                inputs for scalar <b>items</b>, repeatable groups for object ones, held between <b>minItems</b> and
                <b>maxItems</b>. The values are kept flat by path (<b>venue.city</b>, <b>tags[0]</b>, <b>speakers[1].name</b>),
                and <b>OnSubmitJson</b> puts the shape back together.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm Definition="eventForm" OnSubmitJson="json => eventJson = json" />
            <br />
            <BitAiJsonView Value="eventJson" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Streaming schema" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode" CodeFiles="@example7CodeFiles" Id="example7">
            <div>
                A model streams its schema as partial JSON. Rebuilt from the part on every delta, the definition grows field by
                field, and the form seeds each field once: a field that streams in later never overwrites what the user already
                typed. The scripted transport here proposes a booking form - start typing in it while it is still arriving. <b>Busy</b>
                holds the submit back until the whole schema is in, so a field that has not arrived yet cannot be skipped.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitButton OnClick="ProposeBookingAsync" Disabled="proposalSession.IsGenerating">Book a table for Friday</BitButton>
            <br /><br />
            @if (ProposedForm is { } proposed)
            {
                <BitAiForm Definition="proposed" Busy="proposalSession.IsGenerating" Submitted="proposalSubmitted" OnSubmit="values => proposalSubmitted = true" />
            }
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Actions & state" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
            <div>
                <b>SubmitLabel</b> and <b>CancelLabel</b> of the definition name the buttons. Cancel is shown on a form with an
                <b>OnCancel</b>, which it raises (an empty <b>CancelLabel</b> hides it all the same); the other forms of this
                page have none, and so no Cancel. <b>Busy</b> turns the actions off while the submission is in
                flight; <b>Submitted</b> replaces them with a confirmation once it is done. <b>Values</b> reads what the user has
                typed so far, without submitting. A <b>Disabled</b> form turns every input and action off.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm @ref="feedbackFormRef"
                       Definition="feedbackForm"
                       Busy="feedbackBusy"
                       Submitted="feedbackSubmitted"
                       OnSubmit="SendFeedbackAsync"
                       OnCancel="CancelFeedback" />
            <br />
            <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="ReadValues">Read the values</BitButton>
            <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Outline" OnClick="StartOver">Start over</BitButton>
            <br /><br />
            <div>@feedbackStatus</div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm Definition="contactForm" Disabled />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example9CsharpCode" Id="example9">
            <div>
                <b>BitParams</b> with a <b>BitAiFormParams</b> sets the <b>Classes</b> and <b>Styles</b> of the parts - and the
                parameters every component shares, such as <b>Disabled</b> or <b>Dir</b> - of every form inside it, rather than
                the definition and the callbacks of a single form. A form keeps what it sets itself: the second one gives
                <b>Styles</b> of its own, so the cascaded ones do not reach it.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitParams Parameters="formParams">
                <BitAiForm Definition="contactForm" />
                <br />
                <BitAiForm Definition="feedbackForm" Styles="@(new() { Title = "font-style: italic" })" />
            </BitParams>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example10CsharpCode" Id="example10">
            <div>
                <b>Style</b> and <b>Class</b> reach the root, <b>Styles</b> and <b>Classes</b> each part (the buttons take the
                class-styles of BitButton). The inputs are core components, restyled through their own variables. The public
                <b>--bit-AiForm-*</b> variables (see the CSS variables table) inherit, so set on <b>:root</b>, a container or a
                form's <b>Style</b> they re-skin every form below.
            </div>
            <br />
            @* A plain element of this page for the scoped ::deep rules of the custom classes to anchor on. *@
            <div>
                <BitAiForm Definition="contactForm"
                           Style="max-width: 28rem"
                           Styles="@(new() { Root = "background-color: #1e1e2e1a", Title = "color: #8a2be2", SubmitButton = new() { Root = "border-radius: 1rem" } })" />
                <br />
                <BitAiForm Definition="eventForm" Classes="@(new() { Root = "custom-form", Group = "custom-group", Legend = "custom-legend" })" />
                <br />
                <div style="--bit-AiForm-background: transparent; --bit-AiForm-border-color: #d2691e; --bit-AiForm-radius: 0; --bit-AiForm-actions-justify: flex-start; --bit-AiForm-title-font-size: 1.25rem">
                    <BitAiForm Definition="contactForm" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example11RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example11CsharpCode" Id="example11">
            <div>
                In right-to-left text the fields, the groups and the actions read from the right, whether the direction comes
                from <b>Dir</b> or from a <b>dir</b> attribute around the form.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiForm Dir="BitDir.Rtl" Definition="persianForm" />
            <br />
            <div dir="rtl">
                <BitAiForm Definition="persianForm" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>
</DemoPage>
